  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Titus",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 1,
    "summary": "Eternal life was promised before the world began—The qualifications of bishops are given—Unto the pure, all things are pure.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Paul, a servant of God, and an apostle of Jesus Christ, according to the faith of God’s elect, and the acknowledging of the truth which is after godliness;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Servant."
          },
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "TG Apostles."
          },
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "TG Election."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In hope of eternal life, which God, that cannot lie, promised before the world began;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "TG Hope."
          },
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "TG Salvation, Plan of."
          },
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG God, Perfection of; Lying."
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 61,
            "text": "2 Tim. 1:1; Abr. 3:26."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But hath in due times manifested his word through preaching, which is committed unto me according to the commandment of God our Saviour;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "To Titus, mine own son after the common faith: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ our Saviour.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "GR a true son according to."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 64
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For this cause left I thee in Crete, that thou shouldest set in order the things that are wanting, and ordain elders in every city, as I had appointed thee:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "TG Order."
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 109,
            "text": "TG Priesthood, Authority; Priesthood, Ordination."
          },
          {
            "start": 110,
            "end": 116,
            "text": "TG Church Organization; Elder, Melchizedek Priesthood."
          },
          {
            "start": 141,
            "end": 150,
            "text": "GR directed, ordered."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If any be blameless, the husband of one wife, having faithful children not accused of riot or unruly.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 100,
            "text": "GR debauchery or insubordination."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For a bishop must be blameless, as the steward of God; not selfwilled, not soon angry, not given to wine, no striker, not given to filthy lucre;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "TG Bishop; Leadership."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "TG Delegation of Responsibility; Stewardship."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "GR obstinate, arrogant."
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 85,
            "text": "TG Anger."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But a lover of hospitality, a lover of good men, sober, just, holy, temperate;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Hospitality."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "GR what is good."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "GR self-controlled. TG Temperance."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Holding fast the faithful word as he hath been taught, that he may be able by sound doctrine both to exhort and to convince the gainsayers.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 115,
            "end": 123,
            "text": "D&C 11:21."
          },
          {
            "start": 128,
            "end": 138,
            "text": "GR those who deny, contradict."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For there are many unruly and vain talkers and deceivers, specially they of the circumcision:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "GR idle speakers, disputers."
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "TG Apostasy of the Early Christian Church."
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 92,
            "text": "TG Circumcision."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whose mouths must be stopped, who subvert whole houses, teaching things which they ought not, for filthy lucre’s sake.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 105,
            "end": 112,
            "text": "1 Tim. 6:5; Mosiah 29:40; Alma 11:24."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "One of themselves, even a prophet of their own, said, The Cretians are alway liars, evil beasts, slow bellies.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 109,
            "text": "GR lazy gluttons."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 23
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "This witness is true. Wherefore rebuke them sharply, that they may be sound in the faith;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "D&C 84:117 (87, 117)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Not giving heed to Jewish fables, and commandments of men, that turn from the truth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "1 Tim. 1:4."
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "Matt. 15:9; Col. 2:22; D&C 3:6 (6–7); 45:29; 46:7; JS—H 1:19."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "GR who reject, repudiate the truth."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Unto the pure all things are pure: but unto them that are defiled and unbelieving is nothing pure; but even their mind and conscience is defiled.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "JST Titus 1:15 Unto the pure, let all things be pure …"
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "TG Purity."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "TG Pollution."
          },
          {
            "start": 114,
            "end": 118,
            "text": "Luke 11:39 (39–41). TG Mind."
          },
          {
            "start": 123,
            "end": 133,
            "text": "TG Conscience."
          },
          {
            "start": 137,
            "end": 144,
            "text": "Mark 7:15; 2 Ne. 19:17; D&C 93:35."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 28
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 84
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They profess that they know God; but in works they deny him, being abominable, and disobedient, and unto every good work reprobate.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "Matt. 7:21 (21–23). TG False Prophets; Hypocrisy."
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "Hosea 8:2. TG Ignorance."
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "Matt. 15:8 (7–9)."
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "TG Apostasy of the Early Christian Church."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "TG Disobedience."
          },
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 130,
            "text": "GR unfit, worthless."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
